From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:07:07 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-media: decoder mode: scale wide streams down to
 host-max-width

A 3840x2160 HEVC stream reached the guest as a 3840x2160 RGBA buffer:
33 MB a frame, written by the GPU conversion and then composed by the
guest down to its 1920x1080 display. On the Raspberry Pi 5 that kept
V3D at 99% and 4K60 played at 47 to 48 fps, while the decoder alone
runs at about 120.

host-max-width (q11-048) now applies in decoder mode too. A stream
wider than it reaches the guest at that width, the height following
the aspect ratio: CAPTURE's format, G_FMT after SOURCE_CHANGE and the
S_FMT reply carry that size, normalised as any CAPTURE size is, and
the compose rectangle is scaled by the width's ratio. The GPU
conversion samples the full frame and writes the smaller buffer with
that one ratio (the shader's u_scale, as the proxy's host-nv12 does),
for hardware frames and for software ones (q11-073's NV12 is staged
at the frame's size). It does so only when host-max-width made the
guest's size: a guest that chose another size itself is scaled on the
CPU, axis by axis, as before. A scaled buffer is not offered for
direct scanout (q11-071 shows a buffer 1:1). In decoder mode the
property must be 0 or at least 128, the smallest CAPTURE width. The
two size helpers move to virtio-media.h for the decoder to share.

Measured on the Raspberry Pi 5 8GB (2026-10-16, AOSP's codec tool,
host-max-width=1920, with the next patch applied too): HEVC 3840x2160
60p plays at 56.4 and 60.5 fps with -T (V3D 59 to 74% busy) and
decodes at 72.0 fps with -S, against 47.3 and 48.1 fps (V3D 99.3%)
and 56.3 without; all 896 frames come out, with the source's framing.
HEVC 1080p60 plays at 61.1 fps with V3D 18.7 to 18.9%, H.264 1080p60
at 60.6 fps. H.264 2560x1440 60p reaches the guest at 1920x1080
through the GPU and plays at 39.6 fps, the decode thread taking a
whole core.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
